1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,380
Looks like it's Chuck and his crew.

3
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,000
You lost.

4
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:30,780
Now hand over your Sky Raider.

5
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:32,220
You got played, kid.

6
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,110
That's just a regular Nuclear Fission.

7
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,060
Today, I'm destined for a beautiful encounter.

8
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:37,000
Ah!

9
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,500
Dark clouds!

10
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:43,230
Next up, Mini.

11
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:44,220
Okay, you pass.

12
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Episode 4

13
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:53,500
Behold!

14
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,260
He really had us fooled for a second there.

15
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,180
That guy's a total fraud.

16
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:10,620
We should kick him out of here.

17
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:18,380
Coach, let me try 1 more time!

18
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:20,000
I can definitely do it.

19
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:25,020
He's exhausted. Let him rest a bit.

20
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:27,420
Coach, just give me one more shot!

21
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,380
I know I can do it!

22
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,820
Coach, please, one more chance!

23
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,140
Coach! Coach! Give me 1 more chance!

24
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:35,580
I know I've got this!

25
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:37,980
Just 1 more chance, and I'll nail it for sure!

26
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,860
After a rigorous selection process,

27
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:45,180
I officially announce the
Jianghai High School Official Yo-Yo Team

28
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:47,580
has now been formed!

29
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,020
Yay!

30
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:57,660
After our rigorous selection process,

31
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:01,020
the following students have been
selected for the Jianghai Team.

32
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:02,800
Mark!

33
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Teddy!

34
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,500
Mini!

35
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:06,780
Monica.

36
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,220
Matthew.

37
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:11,100
Mickey and Chuck.

38
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,060
Yes!

39
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,500
Also...

40
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,860
The Jianghai Team will hold an
Intensive Training Camp over Summer Break,

41
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:20,220
and we'll win the Championship
at the Autumn Yo-Yo Tournament!

42
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,380
Mark is being totally unbearable today.

43
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,740
I thought you always admired him.

44
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:33,660
Hmph. That was before.

45
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:37,020
Don't you think he's totally abusing his power today?

46
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:38,900
Right?

47
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:41,820
But I don't really care.

48
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:43,100
Because...

49
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:45,660
I finally had a real, genuine beautiful encounter today.

50
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:46,900
Really?

51
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,980
Wait, you didn't walk into a telephone pole again, did you?

52
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:52,290
I'm not that unlucky!

53
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,780
Let me tell you what happened.

54
00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:00,540
Wow, that's incredible.

55
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,900
Yeah! And because you called to rush me this morning,

56
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:06,300
I didn't get a chance to swap phone numbers with him.

57
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:09,180
Plus, I didn't even have a pen and paper on me.

58
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:11,580
Oh, what a shame!

59
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,500
If it had been me,

60
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:15,420
I would have written my number

61
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:16,860
right on the palm of his hand.

62
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:18,300
And I would have made him

63
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,220
write his number on the palm of my hand, too.

64
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:24,540
Yeah, too bad you weren't the one who met him.

65
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:32,220
Oh man, girls are so immature.

66
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:49,020
Talk about a small World.

67
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,420
That's the guy who ruined our plan last time.

68
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:53,820
Hmph. Let me teach him a lesson.

69
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:58,140
Look, look! That's him!

70
00:04:58,300 --> 00:04:59,580
My beautiful encounter from this morning!

71
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:04,380
Ah, it's him!

72
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,260
He must be here looking for me! Let's go!

73
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:18,300
It's you guys.

74
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,220
What? You came looking for me?

75
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:22,620
Perfect. Then let's go one-on-one.

76
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,410
One-on-one at what?

77
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:25,500
At Yo-Yos, obviously.

78
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,340
Sorry, I'm not interested.

79
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:31,740
It's just a friendly Skills Match.

80
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:35,100
You acted all high and mighty the other day.

81
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:38,940
What's the matter? Now that you're on our turf,

82
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:40,860
are you scared?

83
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,260
This is gonna be good.

84
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,100
What do I have to be scared of?

85
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,500
It's just that I happened not to bring my Yo-Yo today.

86
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:50,940
So how can we play?

87
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,820
Then use mine.

88
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:57,500
It's you.

89
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,380
Wow, you're just a regular Good Samaritan, aren't you?

90
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:07,740
Let's go.

91
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:37,500
Hey, kid. Let's see you do "Lightning Fast" 30 times.

92
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:38,940
Let's see if you've got what it takes.

93
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:42,300
Alright, Let's find out.

94
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,260
40!

95
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,180
Wow, Nice.

96
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:04,860
I want a rematch!

97
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:06,780
Maybe next time.

98
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:29,920
I heard he's the new Transfer
Student who just enrolled today.

99
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:31,740
Yeah, what an amazing Yo-Yo Player!

100
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,140
Looks like the Individual Championship Title

101
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,260
is totally up for grabs now.

102
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:46,620
A Prodigy Transfer Student?

103
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:55,740
Oh, it's him.

104
00:08:58,400 --> 00:08:59,100
What's going on?

105
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:00,540
Who's causing trouble on our turf?

106
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:01,980
Was it Jacky's crew?

107
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,900
No...

108
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:06,780
It's that punk who messed with us last time.

109
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,220
Where'd he go?

110
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,620
He's already gone.

111
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,980
You guys are a real credit to the Jianghai Team.

112
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:20,220
Next time I see him, it won't be so easy.

113
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,500
Sis!

114
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:52,380
Why are you walking so fast?

115
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:53,820
I've got homework to do.

116
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:58,110
Sis, that new kid's Yo-Yo skills
today were pretty impressive,

117
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,580
don't you think?

118
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,420
Sis, stop pretending.

119
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:04,860
I could totally tell.

120
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:06,780
Tell what?

121
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:08,500
Stupid.

122
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Sis,

123
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:12,030
I think the smartest move you made all day

124
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:13,020
was lending him your Yo-Yo.

125
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:14,940
That creates a real connection.

126
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:16,380
A real connection,

127
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:17,820
opens the door for more interactions.

128
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:19,260
and with more interactions,

129
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:21,180
I will definitely help you reel him in.

130
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:23,100
Am I right, Sis?

131
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:27,420
Sis, wait up!

132
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,260
Dad, as of today, I'm officially a student

133
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:32,700
at Jianghai High School.

134
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,580
But I don't really feel a connection to it.

135
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:49,980
Tony.

136
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:52,380
This is premium Oolong tea. Have a taste.

137
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:04,380
Well?

138
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:07,260
Mmm, fragrant.

139
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:08,700
Fragrant, right?

140
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:11,580
Have a seat. I'll go get some more hot water.

141
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,060
Tony, how's the tea?

142
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:37,980
It's good. Really good.

143
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:39,620
Then have another cup.

144
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,580
Tony, Leo's back.

145
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,940
Leo, come over here.

146
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,500
Leo!

147
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:06,300
This is Coach Tony from Jianghai High School.

148
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:08,220
He's been waiting for you for hours.

149
00:12:08,700 --> 00:12:09,500
What?

150
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,500
So, our Team has Officially been formed now.

151
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:14,940
The guy you faced off against today

152
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:16,380
is one of our Team members.

153
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:17,340
I see you've already met.

154
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:19,740
Oh, that was him?

155
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,620
The Jianghai Team is planning to use this Summer Break

156
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,540
for some intense, Boot-Camp-Style Training.

157
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:26,460
I came here today

158
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:27,900
to Officially invite you

159
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:29,820
to join us,

160
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:32,220
so we can fight together to win
the Championship in the upcoming Tournament

161
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:33,180
and bring glory to our school.

162
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:36,060
I just found out

163
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,950
that your father, Mr. Li,

164
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,380
is also an alumni of our Jianghai High School .

165
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:41,820
Yeah, I'm aware.

166
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:44,220
You know? That's wonderful!

167
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:46,920
And I know about you, too.

168
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:49,020
I've looked into your background.

169
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:53,340
Runner-Up in the Junior Division at
the California Chinese Yo-Yo Tournament.

170
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,180
"If your 'Eastern Intuition'

171
00:12:58,020 --> 00:13:00,060
can't surpass my 'Western Speed,'

172
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:04,380
then you will never, ever be able to beat me."

173
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:07,740
I also saw you perform that move

174
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,180
"Flying Leaf."

175
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:11,100
Top-notch Technique.

176
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:15,900
Sir,

177
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:18,780
this Grandson of yours is really something else.

178
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,140
Leo,

179
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,060
I truly believe that with you on board,

180
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:25,500
our Jianghai Team winning the Championship

181
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:26,940
is a sure thing.

182
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:29,340
And what if I say no?

183
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:30,500
Huh?

184
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,180
Why?

185
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:34,620
Because...

186
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,500
I don't want to be Teammates with the guys on your Team.

187
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:48,540
You can stop right there. I saw all this coming.

188
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,460
Just didn't think he'd actually turn me down.

189
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:53,340
Don't lose hope, Tony.

190
00:13:54,280 --> 00:13:55,260
There's still a chance.

191
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:58,140
Trust me on this.

192
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:01,020
Alright. I'm heading out. Thank you.

193
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:02,000
Goodbye.

194
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:03,500
Bye.

195
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:25,980
Matthew.

196
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,870
All it took was one loss

197
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,340
to turn you into this?

198
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:32,220
No, it's Monica. Lately,
every time she opens her mouth,

199
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:34,620
It's "Leo this" and "Leo that" nonstop. So annoying.

200
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:37,020
Who's this Leo guy, anyway?

201
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:40,380
He's that new kid who played
against Matthew the other day.

202
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,300
How does Popcorn know him?

203
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:44,220
She probably did some digging.

204
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:47,100
Is there anything in this World she doesn't know?

205
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,500
That kid's always causing trouble for us.

206
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:52,380
Alright, Matthew.

207
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:53,820
Whoever this Leo guy is,

208
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:57,180
If he wants to act tough again,
I'll show him who's the Boss.

209
00:14:59,000 --> 00:14:59,500
Let's go.

210
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:05,340
Listen up, I've got a major scoop.

211
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,260
We know.

212
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,180
The guy who battled Matthew that day,

213
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:11,580
that mysterious prodigy is named Leo, right?

214
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,500
That's old news.

215
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:16,380
What I'm about to say is gonna blow your minds.

216
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:17,820
No one else knows this.

217
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:19,260
Well, spill it!

218
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,180
It's that...

219
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:22,510
The Summer Training Camp

220
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,580
has been Cancelled.

221
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:24,500
Huh?

222
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,420
Are you serious?

223
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:31,260
Turns out the funding the School gave us for the Camp

224
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:32,700
is nowhere near enough.

225
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:35,580
And Coach Tony's attempts to get Sponsors totally failed.

226
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:38,430
So the original Training Camp plan

227
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:38,940
is dead in the water.

228
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:42,780
Then... then how are we supposed to win the Championship?

229
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:45,180
I heard the Chengnan Team has amazing Gear

230
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:47,580
and they're heading to a Training Camp too.

231
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:52,380
They've got money for training and we've got nothing.

232
00:15:52,540 --> 00:15:54,780
How are we supposed to compete with that?

233
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,620
If the school won't back us up,

234
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,500
then winning the Championship doesn't even matter anymore.

235
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,100
Nonsense!

236
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,260
Don't you guys worry about a thing.

237
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,180
The funding issue for the Jianghai Team

238
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:11,580
has already been resolved.

239
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:15,420
- Yes! That's awesome!
- That's great!

240
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:16,860
Coach Tony, no way.

241
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:19,260
What I heard sounded like a sure thing.

242
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:21,180
Monica.

243
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:22,620
Like the old saying goes,

244
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,540
"All roads lead to Rome."

245
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:26,940
You think a little funding hiccup

246
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,340
could actually stump your Coach Tony?

247
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,260
You really are just a loudmouth.

248
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:34,590
Coach Tony, so are we still sticking to the Original Plan

249
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:35,580
for the summer Training Camp?

250
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:36,990
Of course.

251
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:37,980
Did you lock down a location?

252
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:39,420
Yeah!

253
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:42,780
Alright, I'm making it official right now.

254
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:46,140
In 5 days, the entire Team will head to

255
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:49,020
Falcon Camp for Intensive Closed-Door Training!

256
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:52,350
Everyone, go home and make sure you're fully prepared.

257
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,750
That's awesome! I heard there are little cabins there.

258
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,700
And the scenery is amazing.

259
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:59,100
Plus, I heard the wild vegetables there are delicious.

260
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,420
I really didn't see that coming.

261
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:07,740
Big mistake.

262
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:10,620
Why did I just blurt out the name of such an expensive place?

263
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:12,540
I'm in trouble now.

264
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:21,660
Hello? Dad?

265
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:24,060
I knew it was you.

266
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,940
I figured that's why you two
came home so late last night.

267
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:29,340
Oh, well, here's the thing, Dad.

268
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,750
Both me and my Sister passed

269
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,220
the School's Yo-Yo Team tryouts.

270
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:34,620
We're Officially on the Team now.

271
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:36,540
We were selected out of thousands of applicants!

272
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:39,900
And in 5 days, we're leaving
for the Team's Training Camp.

273
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,340
We're getting ready for it right now.

274
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:44,700
Oh, really? Well, congrats! That's fantastic!

275
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,100
Enough with the chit-chat. Just ask him.

276
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:48,500
Dad.

277
00:17:49,180 --> 00:17:50,460
Do you think you could maybe send us

278
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:52,860
a little something as a reward?

279
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:54,780
No problem.

280
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,180
I'm away right now closing a Business deal.

281
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,580
Just make a list of the gifts you want

282
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,020
and fax it to me another day.

283
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,940
But we won't have enough time!

284
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,340
But I can't get back home right away.

285
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:07,740
Then what are we gonna do?

286
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:09,660
Same plan as always, Mickey.

287
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:12,060
You cover it for now using your Tooth Fund.

288
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:13,980
When I gets back, I'll reimburse you for everything.

289
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:17,340
What? You want to dip into my Tooth Fund again?

290
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,740
You still haven't fully paid me back

291
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,180
for what I covered last time.

292
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:25,020
Alright, alright, we'll discuss it later.

293
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,460
I've got things to do right now.

294
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:27,900
Oh, by the way,

295
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:29,820
when do you guys head out?

296
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:32,220
I'll have my driver take you there when it's time.

297
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:54,300
And one more thing! I almost forgot.

298
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,700
My sunscreen is almost completely out.

299
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,140
Can you add another bottle for me?

300
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:02,460
Sis, I heard eating cucumbers
is really good for your skin.

301
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,380
How about I just bring you some of those instead?

302
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:07,740
Hmph. You cheapskate. It's just the Tooth Fund.

303
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:09,660
What was that?

304
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,060
The Tooth Fund was originally

305
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,940
compensation money because someone knocked out my tooth.

306
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:17,340
Dad specifically gave it to me to use.

307
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:19,260
The fact that I'm even chipping in

308
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:21,180
means you should be thanking me.

309
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:23,100
Then you don't have to be so stingy

310
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:24,960
about the things I'm buying.

311
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,380
Fine, whatever.

312
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:35,100
Look, your sunscreen is the most expensive thing here!

313
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,900
At this rate, I'm gonna be flat broke in no time.

314
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:42,300
Is it really that serious?

315
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,140
You just don't get it 'cause you
don't have to manage the budget.

316
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:48,540
You little miser.

317
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:54,780
I'm exhausted.

318
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:58,140
Mickey, go grab us something cold to drink.

319
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:00,540
Too many cold drinks are bad for your teeth.

320
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,380
Fine, then just get some regular drinks.

321
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:05,340
But Dad said

322
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,740
too many sugary drinks are bad for kids' health.

323
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:11,580
Is regular drinking water okay with you?

324
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,870
You're such a pain. Fine, just wait here for me.

325
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:16,860
I'll be right back.

326
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:17,820
Hurry up!

327
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:14,460
Thanks again for the other day.

